.IX Subsection "biplot"
An R\-style \f(CW\*(C`biplot.prcomp\*(C'\fR for the HashRef returned by \f(CW\*(C`Stats::LikeR::prcomp\*(C'\fR,
drawn through \f(CW\*(C`Matplotlib::Simple\*(C'\fR.
.PP
.Vb 1
\& biplot($prcomp, \*(Aqoutput.file\*(Aq => \*(Aqsvg/biplot.png\*(Aq, top => 20);
.Ve
.PP
Options: \f(CW\*(C`choices\*(C'\fR ([1,2] PCs to plot), \f(CW\*(C`top\*(C'\fR (only arrow the N variables with
the longest loading in that plane; 0 = all), \f(CW\*(C`biplot.scale\*(C'\fR (R\*(Aqs \f(CW\*(C`scale\*(C'\fR, 1 by
default), \f(CW\*(C`trim\*(C'\fR (fraction of the most extreme scores that don\*(Aqt get to set the
frame, 0.01 by default; \f(CW\*(C`trim => 0\*(C'\fR frames every point), \f(CW\*(C`labels\*(C'\fR
(ArrayRef of row names to print instead of points), plus any Matplotlib::Simple
option, which is passed through to \f(CW\*(C`scatter\*(C'\fR \-\- so \f(CW\*(C`scale\*(C'\fR still means what it
means everywhere else in Matplotlib::Simple, the figure size.
